item.content:
Acute otitis media (>
                                    6 months of age
                                 ) caused by Haemophilus influenzae, Moraxella catarrhalis, or Streptococcus pneumoniae.

list.item:
•Community-acquired pneumonia (
   >6 months of age
) due to Chlamydophila pneumoniae, Haemophilus influenzae, Mycoplasma pneumoniae, or Streptococcus pneumoniae in patients appropriate for oral therapy.

•Pharyngitis/tonsillitis (
   >2 years of age
) caused by Streptococcus pyogenes as an alternative to first-line therapy in individuals who cannot use first-line therapy.
